The mark up for this page is fine
https://www.raspberrypi.org/documentation/linux/usage/commands.md

but the style sheet, style.css under wp-content/theme/mind-control has text-transform: uppercase;
These command headings are h3, maybe you could change the tag or the css.

h1, h2, h3, h4, h5, h6 {
    font-weight: 400;
    text-transform: uppercase;
}

The dt-blob files associated with https://github.com/raspberrypi/documentation/blob/master/hardware/computemodule/cmio-display.md need to be updated for CM3. Currently they only work with CM1. 

The blobs on the camera page got updated, but not the display. 
https://www.raspberrypi.org/forums/viewtopic.php?f=108&t=172421&p=1103246 has confirmed that simply adding
```
   pin_defines {
       pin_define@DISPLAY_SDA {
          type = "internal";
          number = <0>;
       };
       pin_define@DISPLAY_SCL {
          type = "internal";
          number = <1>;
       };
       pin_define@DISPLAY_I2C_PORT {
          type="internal";
          number=<0>;
       };
```
appears sufficient. Probably ought to do a slightly more comprehensive test though.

https://www.raspberrypi.org/forums/viewtopic.php?f=66&t=177001

I beleive this is non-trivial so we could do with some instructions.

@spl237 Any thoughts?

Too much sudo;
Use 'tail -F' is more universal than 'tail -f';
Use Ctrl+Z for exit is wrong — use Ctrl+C.

